<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raúl Alfonsín</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a>–<a href="/years/2009">2009</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raúl Alfonsín was an Argentine lawyer and Radical Civic Union politician who served as president from 1983 to 1989, the first elected after the military dictatorship. He set up a commission to investigate the disappeared and allowed the trial of the juntas in 1985. Hyperinflation and military unrest marked his later years, and he handed over power early to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-menem">Carlos Menem</a> in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raul-alfonsin.jpg" alt="Raúl Alfonsín" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidencia de la Nación Argentina · CC BY 2.5 ar · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ra%C3%BAl_Alfons%C3%ADn_con_banda_presidencial_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
